# Data licensing

The **code** in this release is MIT (see LICENSE). The **data** divides by
provenance as follows.

## CC BY-SA 4.0 (required)

Everything derived from Wikipedia. Wikipedia article text is CC BY-SA 4.0, so
this is not a choice.

- `trajectories/*.jsonl` — contain the full text of the retrieved passages
- `annotated/*.jsonl` — contain passage quotations
- `human_audit/*` — the audit sheets contain passage excerpts

(The standalone `corpus/passages.jsonl`, in the dataset repository, is under
the same terms.)

Sources: https://ko.wikipedia.org , https://en.wikipedia.org
Full licence: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

Redistribution and derivative works must preserve the ShareAlike condition and
attribute the source.

## CC0 1.0

Structured data originating from Wikidata, which is released under CC0.

- `dataset/triples.jsonl` — (Subject, Bridge, Answer) triples
- `retrieval/alias_cache.json` — Wikidata label / alias / sitelink cache

Source: https://www.wikidata.org
Full licence: https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/

## Mixed

- `dataset/qa_pairs.jsonl` — the question templates are our own work (MIT); the
  entity surface forms filled into them originate from Wikidata (CC0). The file
  as a whole is distributed under CC BY-SA 4.0.

## Model outputs

The `generated_text` fields in `trajectories/` were produced under each
provider's terms of service. Redistribution here is for research use;
commercial use requires checking the terms of each provider.

The four open-weight models carry their own licences, which the stored
generations inherit — Aya Expanse: CC BY-NC 4.0 plus the C4AI Acceptable Use
Policy (non-commercial); EXAONE 3.5: EXAONE AI Model License Agreement 1.1
(research use); Llama 3.1: Llama 3.1 Community License; Qwen3: Apache-2.0.
No model weights are redistributed.
